# NET-3 pass 1: WP coupling - clients report their resident WP cells (reliable lane, UE ServerUpdateLevelVisibility);
# the gateway's relevant set per connection = own pawn + dynamic objects whose grid cell the client has resident +
# stable objects of resident cells (WP grid = relevancy grid, Iris NetObjectGridFilter equivalent); objects that
# leave the set are removed on the client (Remove message) and come back with full state when the cell returns.
# World delta table in the store (destroyed / detached / changed stable ids), replayed to a client when it loads a
# cell; server console `destroy <id>`. Rotation quantization grid is centred (odd level count) so identity is exact.
# Runner: <scratch>/NET-3/run_all.sh (base NET-2 run_net2.sh): A = Editor, B = DesertNetProbe bot; A's pawn is
# moved by the server console `transform <A pawn> ...` (1.5 km away, then back).
# Дано: DesertServer + Editor client A and bot B from task/NET-3 on WP_Protocol.
# Тогда [net3_start] net3-start/clientA_start.png: A's frame shows B's pawn and the barrel at the start.
# Когда: A goes 1.5 km away; server console `destroy <barrel id>`.
# Тогда [net3_far] net3-far/clientA_far.png: no B pawn; A's log shows the start cells unloaded and B removed from relevancy.
# Когда: A returns to the start.
# Тогда [net3_back] net3-back/clientA_back.png: B's pawn again and no barrel; server log shows the delta replayed for that cell.
